at the same time as the Foundation, but fortunately SCP-3056-1 instances could be recovered by the Foundation without incident. Infected animals were destroyed with the help of Global Occult Coalition operatives.</p> <div class="footnotes-footer"> <div class="title">Footnotes</div> <div class="footnote-footer" id="footnote-408591-1"><a href="javascript:;" >1</a>. A family of RNA virus that includes Influenza A, Influenza B, Influenza C, and Influenza D.</div> <div class="footnote-footer" id="footnote-408591-2"><a href="javascript:;" >2</a>. A part of virus reproduction cycles which results in the destruction of the infected cells</div> <div class="footnote-footer" id="footnote-408591-3"><a href="javascript:;" >3</a>. Process to replace failing old cells with new, healthy cells</div> <div class="footnote-footer" id="footnote-408591-4"><a href="javascript:;" >4</a>. (NH<sub>4</sub>MgPO<sub>4</sub>.6H<sub>2</sub>O), a mineral commonly found in the urine of mammals infected with urea-splitting bacterium</div> </div> <div class="footer-wikiwalk-nav"> <div style="text-align: center;"> <p>&#171; <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-3055">SCP-3055</a> | SCP-3056 | <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-3057">SCP-3057</a> &#187;</p> </div> </div> <p>by <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/rigen" ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=2826105&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1606508050" alt="Rigen" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=2826105)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/rigen" >Rigen</a></span></p> 
